WORDING CARRIED FROM SOURCES THAT STATE NO LICENCE

Two vocabularies are reproduced exactly, because they are identifiers a
reader has to type character for character rather than expression:
FILE, PACKAGE, WIRE_JSON and WIRE from the Buf breaking-change rule
categories (EV-0135), and BACKWARD, FORWARD, FULL and NONE from
Confluent Schema Registry compatibility (EV-0139). Both pages were read
on 2026-08-08 and both were found to state no reuse licence, so no
licence asks for attribution here. They are named because their wording
is carried and a reader of this file should be told so.


SOURCES WHOSE LICENCE NOBODY HAS CONFIRMED

registry/LICENCE_RESIDUALS.md lists them in full, by evidence id, split
between the sources that state no licence and the sources whose licence
was never recorded. Read that file before reusing anything that rests
on one of them. Its counts were compiled from a ledger of 449 records
and the ledger now holds 504, so its tables are behind the ledger by
the rows the last import added.


WHAT THE SWEEP DID AND DID NOT DO

It re-fetched nothing, so it confirmed no licence. It read the pack
prose and the licence values already recorded in registry/evidence.json
and sorted them into what somebody observed and what somebody asserted.
Ninety of the 504 licence lines carry an observation date. The rest are
the recording agent's word for it.

It covered all twenty-one packs. The agentic-swarm sweep ran last, over
62 cited ids: it found no carried expression, and it recorded that 46 of
its rows arrived in the 2026-08-10 import and carry a licence nobody has
yet observed at source.

A scan that finds no carried passage proves what was read, not what
exists. No claim of completeness is made for it.
